{"id": "sevt_01V5He3Bo8mBmvgpKBoMiHMc", "content": [{"text": "Root cause: `49333d6` turned a batched item query into one query per order row. It is still deployed and has not been rolled back.\n\n**Evidence**\n- **Deploys:** two checkout deploys sit near the spike, but only one lines up.\n  - `dcaf6a6` (14:03) caused its own spike at 14:03 and was rolled back at 14:07. p99 returned to normal.\n  - `9ea808a` (14:33) was rolled back at 14:35. p99 was already climbing before it and kept climbing after, so it isn't the cause.\n  - `49333d6` (\"tidy order summary helpers\") deployed at 14:15. p99 was about 64 ms at 14:15 and 125 ms at 14:16.\n- **Metrics:** p99 then climbed steadily from about 125 ms at 14:16 to about 414 ms at 14:37. That is a ramp, not a step. Checkout `db_pool_utilization` rose in step with it, from about 0.19 to 0.71 over the same period.\n- **Spike:** p99 jumped to about 3,757 ms at 14:38 and about 4,036 ms at 14:39, and stayed around 4 s after that. Pool utilization reached 1.0 at 14:46 and stayed there. The 14:38 step is probably the pool nearing saturation under load, but I didn't find a log line that explains it.\n- **Diff:** in `CheckoutSummaryHandler.build_summary`, a single `OrderItem ... order_id__in=ids` query grouped in memory became a loop that runs `OrderItem.objects.filter(order_id=order.order_id)` for each order. That is the N+1 pattern the runbook lists first.\n- **Log:** the per-row query `SELECT * FROM order_items WHERE order_id = ?` appears 3,312 times in `app.log`. The debug line comes from the new code, so these should all be from the two checkout deploys. Per-minute counts rose from about 30 in the 14:19\u201314:35 samples to about 100\u2013126 from 14:39. Those are sampled minutes, not every minute.\n\n**Recommended action:** roll back `49333d6`, or restore the batched query.\n\n> **Root cause:** `49333d6` \u2014 `build_summary` now queries `order_items` once per open order instead of once per request (N+1). This pushed load on the checkout DB pool until it saturated and p99 spiked around 14:38\u201314:39.", "type": "text"}], "processed_at": "2026-10-14T05:44:24.710626Z", "type": "agent.message"}
